T* (In this book a number of dialects are used, to wit: the Missouri negro) Tj
T* (dialect; the extremest form of the backwoods Southwestern dialect; the) Tj
T* (ordinary ?Pike County? dialect; and four modified varieties of this) Tj
T* (last. The shadings have not been done in a haphazard fashion, or by) Tj
T* (guesswork; but painstakingly, and with the trustworthy guidance and) Tj
T* (support of personal familiarity with these several forms of speech.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I make this explanation for the reason that without it many readers) Tj
T* (would suppose that all these characters were trying to talk alike and) Tj
T* (not succeeding.) Tj
