T* (You don?t know about me without you have read a book by the name of The) Tj
T* (Adventures of Tom Sawyer; but that ain?t no matter. That book was made) Tj
T* (by Mr. Mark Twain, and he told the truth, mainly. There was things) Tj
T* (which he stretched, but mainly he told the truth. That is nothing. I) Tj
T* (never seen anybody but lied one time or another, without it was Aunt) Tj
T* (Polly, or the widow, or maybe Mary. Aunt Polly?Tom?s Aunt Polly, she) Tj
T* (is?and Mary, and the Widow Douglas is all told about in that book,) Tj
T* (which is mostly a true book, with some stretchers, as I said before.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Now the way that the book winds up is this: Tom and me found the money) Tj
T* (that the robbers hid in the cave, and it made us rich. We got six) Tj
T* (thousand dollars apiece?all gold. It was an awful sight of money when) Tj
T* (it was piled up. Well, Judge Thatcher he took it and put it out at) Tj
T* (interest, and it fetched us a dollar a day apiece all the year) Tj
T* (round?more than a body could tell what to do with. The Widow Douglas) Tj
T* (she took me for her son, and allowed she would sivilize me; but it was) Tj
T* (rough living in the house all the time, considering how dismal regular) Tj
